WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.520
- Knights of the Round Table
were expected to adhere

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.580
to a strict moral standard
of piety, honor, bravery,

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.800
and courtesy called chivalry.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.900
But considering that they
often spent their days

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.810
killing and rampaging at
the behest of their Lord,

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:13.710
that must have required

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.140
some next level compartmentalization.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.670
This duality is reflected

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.740
in the various versions of a key figure

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.530
who appears in Arthurian
legends throughout history,

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:23.760
Sir Gawain.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.920
In some stories, Gawain is the embodiment

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.360
of chivalry excellence.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.940
He rescues maidens, masterminds quests,

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.620
and takes out pirates.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.920
In others, Gawain is
very much the anti-hero,

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.500
Even inciting the fall of King Arthur.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.690
This vacillation of Gawain's character

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.370
is most clearly on display

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.580
in what is perhaps the most
well-known Arthurian legend,

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.567
the 14th century chivalric poem,

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.450
"Sir Gawain and the Green Knight."

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.460
The story is a generally favorable account

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.840
of Gawain's character,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.170
but it also lays bare the
ambiguities of his position.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.630
Is Gawain's conflicted
depiction in "The Green Night"

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.640
a criticism of chivalry and heroism

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.410
as it was known at the time.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.683
Perhaps it is a commentary on
the human condition at large.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.420
(dramatic music)

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.517
Written anonymously and
rediscovered centuries later,

00:01:12.517 --> 00:01:13.860
"Sir Gawain and the Green Night"

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.350
is set at Christmastime
and involves an intruder,

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.530
and that's where the
similarities to "Home Alone" end.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.600
While Arthur and his knights are feasting,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.850
they're interrupted by
a giant green knight

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.300
in green garments riding a
green horse right into the hall.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.760
The green knight claims
he seeks no violence,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.290
only a game.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:34.530
He invites someone to
strike him with his own ax,

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:35.430
and in return,

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.960
the volunteer must consent

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.670
to the green knight striking him

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.800
in one year and one day's time.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.970
So who's it gonna be?

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.800
Arthur is about to rise to the challenge

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.920
to save face until the
loyal Gawain steps in.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.740
For some reason, Gawain
decides to go big or go home.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.180
He rolls a natural 20

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.550
and chops the Green
Knight's head clean off.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:54.690
Game over, right?

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.180
Well, imagine his surprise
when the green knight

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.460
calmly scoops up his laughing head

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.640
and orders going to find him
at the Green Chapel next year

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.320
where he will repay the blow.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.450
It may not sound like
something that would catch on,

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.790
but this game actually has a name.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:11.130
Popularized in Celtic
and medieval mythology,

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.620
the beheading game, yes, really,

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.450
usually involves a young warrior

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.690
being invited to behead
and submit to a beheading,

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:21.270
kind of like an ultra
stakes power slap league.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:22.710
In a famous Irish myth,

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.240
evil lord Bricriu invites

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.460
three of Ireland's best heroes to dinner

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.410
and pits them against each other.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.700
For their final challenge,

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.880
a mysterious warrior orders
them to chop off his head

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.390
and come back the next night
for him to return the blow.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:39.390
- So you want us to chop your head off?

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.190
- Yes, please.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:42.330
- But why?

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.410
- I guess you could say,

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:46.113
I want to stay ahead of the game.

00:02:47.034 --> 00:02:49.560
(rock music)

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.210
- [Emily] Only one of
the heroes, Cu Chulainn,

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.890
shout out to our Cu Chulainn episode,

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:56.163
shows up cementing his
status as the winner.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.597
- Guess that makes me head of the class.

00:03:01.597 --> 00:03:04.590
(rock music)

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:05.490
- [Emily] In another legend,

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:06.630
Arthur's night Caradoc

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.790
is obliged to behead a hooded stranger

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.200
and submit to a beheading.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.960
The beheading game is like
the ultimate test of honor.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.030
Will you keep your word to play the game

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.500
even if it means your death?

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.450
Meanwhile, the people on my trivia team

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:21.390
have always some kind of
excuse for not showing up,

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.610
even though I made it very clear

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.590
that pub trivia is a commitment.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:26.940
After a very anxious year,

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.860
Gawain must either stick
to the terms of the game

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:29.880
or lose his honor.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.620
So he rides out to meet his fate.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.360
After encountering a variety of enemies

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.090
and marvels that are not
described, but trust us,

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:36.923
they were amazing,

00:03:36.923 --> 00:03:39.960
he arrives at the grand castle
of Lord and Lady Bertilak.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.690
The Bertilaks tell him that
he's close to the Green Chapel,

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:45.450
but offer to let him rest
up with them for a few days.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.700
Gawain's in no rush to
get his head chopped off,

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.440
so he happily accepts

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.330
not knowing that he's just walked into

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.100
yet another bizarre game.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.770
Lord Bertilak declares that
he will go hunting every day

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.570
and share his spoils with Gawain.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.530
But in return,

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.330
Gawain must give the Lord whatever

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:02.790
he's received during
his day at the castle.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:03.780
On the first day,

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.300
Lady Bertilak sneaks
into Gawain's chambers

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.070
and attempts to seduce him.

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.710
He rebuffs her politely
with a chaste kiss.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:12.030
When the Lord returns from the hunt,

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:13.530
he shares a deer with Gawain

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:16.020
and Gawain gives him a single kiss.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.960
On the second day, Gawain
permits two kisses from the lady,

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.660
which he passes on to the
lord in exchange for a boar.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.308
On the third day,

00:04:23.308 --> 00:04:24.750
the lady lavish is
Gawain with three kisses

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.430
and something extra.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:27.960
I know you think we're
gonna know this is going,

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.310
but I promise you it's not.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.280
A magical green and gold girdle,

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.870
which she promises will protect him

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:34.800
from the green night.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.200
When the Lord returns,
Gawain has a dilemma.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.870
Keeping the girdle secret
would break his promise,

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.280
but might save his life

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.770
and avoid a very awkward conversation.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:45.090
Like many mythical heroes,

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.640
Gawain is constantly
trying to prove his worth,

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.960
but gets confused by games

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.930
with arbitrary rules and
unclear expectations.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:52.800
In medieval times,

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.350
there was a fine line
between games and violence.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.640
Okay, still kind of true.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.770
Dueling and hunting were recreational,

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.740
but they were also part of
a knight's violent duties.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.630
By participating in
both the beheading game

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:04.860
and a hunting game,

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.300
Gawain is simultaneously

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.640
navigating the worlds
of violence and sport

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.140
and apparently sex.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:11.790
And by accepting the spoils of the hunt

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:12.840
while keeping the girdle,

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.400
he sacrifices his honor.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.530
Finally, Gawain arrives
at the Green Chapel,

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:19.860
an uncanny grassy cave and
confronts the green knight.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:20.700
Despite his fear,

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:23.310
he kneels at the giant's
feet and offers his neck

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.270
as promised,

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:26.640
the green knight lifts
his ax above his head,

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.740
swings it down at Gawain's neck,

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:31.650
but only nicks him drawing
a few drops of blood.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:33.060
Gawain is in shock,

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.010
but the green knight burst out laughing

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:37.200
and commends Gawain for
upholding the bargain.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.230
He reveals himself to be
none other than Lord Bertilak

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:43.620
disguised by the magic of the
old sorceress Morgan le Fay

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.120
to test Arthur's knights.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.920
It was all a prank, I guess.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:49.260
This mirrors the ending
of other beheading games

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:50.340
and "Bricriu's Feast,"

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:53.040
Cu Chulainn is spared on
account of his bravery

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.930
while Paradox's story ends with his enemy

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:56.490
striking him with a blunt sword

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.140
and praising him for his courage.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.739
On the one hand,

00:05:59.739 --> 00:06:01.050
these stories make light
of the hero's struggle

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.670
by turning a serious bargain

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.320
into a courtly jest.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:05.160
On the other,

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:07.320
they can be read as a critique of heroism

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.600
and its hollow violent nature.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.610
The story of Gawain and the green knight

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:13.260
shares this dual meaning.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.720
It pokes fun at lofty chivalric standards,

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.120
but it also interrogates the impossibility

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.260
of these standards.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:23.142
While Gawain should be proud
of mostly passing the test,

00:06:23.142 --> 00:06:24.780
he feels like a coward
for breaking his word

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:25.710
about the girdle

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:28.440
and arrives back at
court an emotional wreck.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:29.273
But luckily,

00:06:29.273 --> 00:06:31.950
he's got his round table
bros to lift him back up.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.120
As far as they're concerned,

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.910
he survived a terrifying
ordeal with his reputation,

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.470
more or less intact.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:39.930
They even all start wearing
green and gold girdles

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:41.340
to celebrate him.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.990
- Gawain's our hero.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:44.092
- Thanks.

00:06:44.092 --> 00:06:44.925
Does my epic beard help?

00:06:44.925 --> 00:06:46.140
- Absolutely, yes.

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:47.990
Green and gold girdle crew represent.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:51.447
(both laugh)

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:00.690
- Lord and Lady Bertilak

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.992
have a really messed up relationship.

00:07:02.992 --> 00:07:04.680
- Yeah.

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:07.860
- Gawain's hero status
is a Christmas miracle.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.080
The Christmas setting is no accident.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.480
It highlights another
tension that poor Gawain

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:13.680
has to navigate.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.080
That between Christian and pagan worlds.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.720
A Christian holiday is
literally interrupted

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:21.030
by an explicitly pagan figure,

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:24.090
with his green skin, wild
beard, and bare chest,

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.310
the green night clearly represents nature.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.680
And resembles the mythical green man,

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:30.810
a face encased in leaves that appears

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:33.600
in ancient artwork from
India to the British Isles.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:36.330
Green was also the color of
witchcraft and the devil,

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.250
and there's something
definitely supernatural

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:40.680
about a giant who can pick
up his own severed head.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.450
Magic in the form of the girdle

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:46.290
is also what punctures Gawain's
otherwise watertight honor.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:47.970
And yet, the test of Gawain's honor

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:50.430
is only possible because of sorcery,

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:52.710
which enables the
transformation of Lord Bertilak

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:54.270
into a green giant.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:56.280
These chaotic circumstances

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.520
reveal the entanglement of
paganism and Christianity,

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:01.140
which shaped the medieval worldview.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:03.240
No wonder Gawain is confused.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:06.270
Gawain's inconsistency can be
attributed to his character

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:07.950
or lack thereof.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:09.660
The lack of a significant trait

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.700
leaves him open to our projections,

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:12.930
but it's also what makes him

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:15.150
the most human of Arthur's knights.

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:15.983
In the end,

00:08:15.983 --> 00:08:18.420
it's hard not to feel a
little sorry for Gawain.

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:19.830
By just trying to do the right thing,

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.320
he got tricked into
volunteering for beheading,

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:25.260
made a treacherous journey
towards his own certain death.

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:28.140
Got sucked into an eccentric
couple's weird sex games

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.120
all to get laughed at by the green knight.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:33.060
Still, Gawain arguably
manages to stay honorable

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:35.160
along the way except for the girdle.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.380
But come on, who wouldn't
wanna keep the girdle?

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:40.267
Later depictions of Gawain
have shared the sympathy.

00:08:40.267 --> 00:08:42.270
"The Once and Future King" fantasy novels

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.880
concoct a traumatic childhood for Gawain.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.237
While the recent film adaptation,

00:08:46.237 --> 00:08:49.350
"The Green Knight" portrays
him as a very human hero,

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:52.470
trying to make the best
of baffling circumstances.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:53.303
In the comic,

00:08:53.303 --> 00:08:55.620
"Once and Future"
Arthurian legend is retold

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:59.070
in a modern day exploration
of the power of storytelling

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:01.260
with Gawain's mantle taken up by Rose,

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:03.090
one of the female protagonists.

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:04.980
While these expansions to Gawain lore

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.620
and modern day mythmaking
more explicitly comment

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:10.530
on changing attitudes
towards gender and heroism,

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:13.200
the internal conflicts at
the core of the narrative

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.870
continue to reflect the
complexity of humanity

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:17.400
and our brutal world.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:20.250
We might not play the beheading
game at parties anymore,

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.590
but the tension between
entertainment and violence

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:24.630
is still very much a part of culture.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.310
The legends of Gawain are a testament

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:28.050
that even a night of the Roundtable

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:31.620
can be susceptible to pitfalls,
mistakes, and human error.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:34.200
Not to mention the
hypocrisies of chivalry,

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:37.320
which the original anonymous
author seemed to recognize.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:39.600
Ultimately, Gawain is a
hero who is thoroughly

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.340
shaped by the world around him.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.370
His challenge lies in
upholding cultural norms,

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.920
but his power lies in exposing the cracks

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:50.010
and contradictions that
underlie those norms.

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:51.090
So if you've been following along

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.830
for this season of "Fate and Fabled,"

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.470
we're doing our favorite Pantheon picks.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.750
So for my pick for this episode,

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:00.360
I'm going with the Morrigan.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:01.590
- Ooh.

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:02.760
Nice choice.
- Thank you.

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:04.020
- The Morrigan, I just think

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:05.730
is really interesting perspective wise,

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:07.800
'cause she's one and many,

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:09.750
she can also shapeshift into a crow.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.100
And you know how much I love birds.

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:12.780
So the Morrigan's my pick.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:13.613
- Yeah, that's great.

00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:14.446
Great pick.

00:10:14.446 --> 00:10:16.260
- [Emily] Stay tuned for our next episode

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.600
and you'll get to hear
our next Pantheon pick.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:21.450
Before you go, we wanna
hear your feedback.

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:23.220
Every year, PBS Digital Studios

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.300
surveys our audience

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.760
helping us understand
what you enjoy on YouTube

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:29.310
and what you would want
to see us make more of.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:31.380
You also get to vote on new show ideas.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:33.120
So it'd be great if "Fate and Fabled" fans

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:34.920
were well represented in the polls.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.390
There's a link in the description.

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:37.353
Thanks in advance.

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:40.380
- [Speaker] Whoa.

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:41.883
- Do I then fall over?

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.526
- [Speaker] I laughed.

00:10:44.526 --> 00:10:46.083
Yeah, there you go.

00:10:46.083 --> 00:10:48.250
- Green and gold girdle...

